Process execution records summarize the final status of a process crunching
a blob. The seven, tab separated fields are as follows:

	start_time		#  start time in rfc3339 nano format
	flow_seq		#  uint64
	command_tag		#  [^a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,31}
	process_id		#  0 < 2^64
	exit_class		#  {OK,ERR,SIG,NOPS}
	blob			#  udig
	exit_code		#  0 <= 255
	wall_duration		#  elapsed wall time in seconds, as sec.nsec
	user_seconds		#  rusage SELF of cpu in user space, as sec.msec
	sys_seconds		#  rusage SELF of cpu in kernel, as sec.msec

Typically the xdr records are written into spool/<floq-server>.xdr
